074 "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,0).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $3$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/39/39266e152f7a52ee6cf56ad872704a110765e22c5d3fcea6f4b4c7565276ee24.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,0).$" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435929 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435927 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435929 1069 "q-80813" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435929 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435929 1071 "Which of the following are subsets of ${Q}_{0}^{+}$ (the set of non-negative rational numbers)?\n\nI. ${Z}^{-}$ (the set of negative integers)\n\nII. $N$\n\nIII. ${Z}_{0}^{+}$ (the set of non-negative integers)" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435929 1072 #uuid "751ef612-b871-5a13-b5db-9f9345197dd4" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435929 1074 "$A$ is a subset of $B$ if every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect the given choices.\n\n- ${Z}^{-}$ is not a subset of ${Q}_{0}^{+}.$ For example, $-1\\in {Z}^{-}$ but $-1\\notin {Q}_{0}^{+}.$\n\n- $N$ is a subset of ${Q}^{+}.$ Indeed, every natural number is also a positive rational number.\n\n- ${Z}_{0}^{+}$ is a subset of ${Q}_{0}^{+}.$ Indeed, every positive integer is also a positive rational number. Notice also that  $0$ is in both  ${Z}_{0}^{+}$ and ${Q}_{0}^{+}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III  only\"." 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435930 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435926 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435930 1069 "q-102697" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435930 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435930 1071 "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=6t-2$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=-1\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=1\\,\\text{s}$, calculate the speed of the particle at the moment $t=3\\,\\text{s}.$" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435930 1072 #uuid "856c86c0-9a1d-541f-bee9-93df07ee1d90" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435930 1074 "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (6t-2)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-2t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(1)=-1.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =3(1)^{2}-2(1)+C \\\\ -1 & =3-2+C \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=3{t}^{2}-2t-2.$\n\nWe evaluate the velocity at time $t=3\\,\\text{s}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =3(3)^{2}-2(3)-2 \\\\  & =27-6-2 \\\\  & =19\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the speed is equal to $|v(t)|,$ we conclude that the speed of the particle is $19\\,\\text{m/s}.$" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435931 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435925 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435931 1069 "q-129384" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435931 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435931 1071 "Calculate $\\text{Var}[{2}^{k}]$ where $k$ is a constant." 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435931 1072 #uuid "d437ae95-9320-5f38-963e-97e760ec1b57" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435931 1074 "Recall that for any constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[a]=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[{2}^{k}]=0.\n$$" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435932 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435934 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435932 1062 #uuid "11e9ef78-3c1d-5304-92fe-98c32e4f645a" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435932 1063 #edb/ref 17592186241013 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435933 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435939 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435933 1062 #uuid "2e9b0e94-e8c8-557f-b348-b08fccb363e6" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435933 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435930 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435934 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435933 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435934 1062 #uuid "67d9c9df-eb88-5700-a91b-21973dca0f26" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435934 1063 #edb/ref 17592186362318 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435935 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435937 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435935 1062 #uuid "6ecb1c55-62bb-540c-82e8-c73c10ae3111" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435935 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435929 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435936 1062 #uuid "b38c0521-a094-53a3-8a24-4119dcd45c0a" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435936 1063 #edb/ref 17592186338872 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435937 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435940 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435937 1062 #uuid "c44e9c92-4a17-5e6c-8c86-3e098f699c9a" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435937 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435931 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435938 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435935 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435938 1062 #uuid "ca3a1e0a-5bd3-54a7-beb6-fad92e68d746" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435938 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435928 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435939 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435936 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435939 1062 #uuid "f7704b65-91b6-56c9-bef6-9023ce8a9784" 13194139534784 17592186045417 true] [17592186435939 